>
  <h1>Documentation</h1>
  <p>
    flowlane automates the architecture of your workflow: tickets, branches, and pull requests for Azure
    DevOps, GitHub, and Jira — without leaving the terminal. Everything below is maintained alongside the
    source in this repo.
  </p>

  <h2>Getting started</h2>
  <p>
    One global install, one interactive wizard, then flow. <code>npm install -g flowlane</code>, run
    <code>flowlane init</code>, and flowlane writes its config to <code>~/.config/flowlane/config.json</code>.
  </p>

  <h3>Quick links</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="/docs/install">Install &amp; prerequisites</a> — Node 18+, git, tokens, first setup.</li>
    <li><a href="/docs/adding-a-provider">Add a provider</a> — extend flowlane to your own platform.</li>
    <li><a href="/docs/reference">Command reference</a> — the full CLI surface.</li>
    <li><a href="/license">License</a> — MIT, free forever.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>The workflow</h2>
  <p>
    flowlane separates <strong>ticketing</strong> from <strong>pull requests / VCS</strong>, so ticket and PR
    providers are configured independently. Pair Jira ticketing with GitHub PRs, or Azure DevOps end-to-end.
  </p>
  <pre><code>flowlane start 14        # branch from a ticket, pushed to origin
flowlane pr 14           # PR with the ticket link attached
flowlane pr review 42    # threads, files, inline comments, votes
flowlane pr complete 42  # merge — board column auto-updates</code></pre>

  <h2>Configuration</h2>
  <p>
    Profiles keep separate credentials per organisation. A <code>.flowlane</code> file in a repository
    overrides the global profile for that repo. Every setting is a <code>flowlane config set</code> away, and
    post-action hooks can open the PR, ping Slack, or launch your editor.
  </p>

  <blockquote>
    "The terminal is where developers are most productive. Don't force them out of it."
  </blockquote>

  <p>
    Something missing? The docs are open source — contribute corrections on
    <a href="https://github.com/Nils-dev-mertens/flowlane" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">GitHub</a>.
  </p>
</DocsLayout>